  "id": "image_krea2_turbo_style_reference",
  "name": "Krea 2 Turbo — generate in the style of 1–3 pictures",
  "description": "Generate a new picture in the STYLE of one to three pictures you supply. Krea 2 Turbo reads the look — palette, material, light, brushwork, grain — from your references and applies it to whatever you describe, rather than copying their content.\n\nOne reference is enough. A second and third are optional and worth adding when the look is more than one thing at once (say a colour palette from one and a material or texture from another) — they are averaged, so three wildly different pictures give a muddle rather than a blend.\n\nDescribe the SUBJECT in the prompt and leave the style to the references: \"a white yeti with horns reading a book\" plus a reference does more than restating the style in words. Style strength controls how hard the reference pulls: 1.0 is the tested setting, lower it towards 0.6 if the subject is being dragged out of shape.\n\nEnhance prompt with AI rewrites your sentence into a longer one with a local LLM before generating — useful from a few words, unnecessary when you have already written a full description.",
  "category": "t2i",
  "tags": [
    "krea2",
    "turbo",
    "style-reference",
    "style-transfer",
    "reference"
  ],
  "promptGuides": [
    {
      "label": "Krea 2 prompting guide",
      "url": "https://github.com/krea-ai/krea-2/blob/main/docs/prompting.md",
      "tip": "Describe the subject and the scene; let the reference pictures carry the style. Krea responds well to plain, concrete sentences."
    }
  ],
